// rustc E0596 at each (twin .rs.txt): cannot borrow `*h.r` as mutable, as
// it is behind a `&` reference. Refused right today: the method-chain
// place `h.me().me().r`, and the assignments `o.p = h.r`, `*o = h.r`,
// `p = h.r` (borrowck.borrow_immutable). RT-284 has a block's
// tail, an if's arms, a match arm in a fn and a closure's result; RT-314
